{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane","id":1470673,"title":"[V5] Alternative Ravnos Bane","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-16T17:41:51-08:00","id":1470673,"title":"[V5] Alternative Ravnos Bane","content":"Okay I'm gonna put this out there, the Ravnos are a good clan. Sadly, this was often overshadowed by a history of stereotyping and bad writing on part of White Wolf. Now with all that said, it is no wonder that V5 felt like it had to change the weakness for V5. That said, it wasn't the best. Seriously being forced to move around or burn sucks! Not only that, but it limits playing Ravnos in V5 to only modern timeline, which is also my issue with Tremere, Salubri, and Banu Haquim. With all that said, here are the two possible alternative weaknesses for Clan Ravnos:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Option 1</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ravnos are <b>slaves</b> to the call of the blood. Whenever a Ravnos suffers from a Compulsion, the dice penalty they suffer is increased by an amount equal to their Bane Severity. Even worse is that the stigma the Ravnos suffer from their reputation is on par with the clanless and thin-blooded, imposing a two-dice penalty to all Social tests against fellow Kindred who know of their infamous lineage. </div> </div> </div>The above weakness is based off of their original weakness found in previous editions. Honestly, I thought of this in the shower and wanted to share.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Option 2</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The words of Caine were clear. Those of the Ravnos clan were to be <b>outcasts</b> and trusted by no one. Anywhere the Ravnos settle quickly develop rumors about the travelers and their supposed misdeeds. After the first few nights in a city, the rumors about the Kindred quickly spread, sowing the seeds of mistrust and fear into both the Kindred and mortal populations alike. The Ravnos suffer a dice penalty to all Social test dice pools against anyone, mortal or otherwise, who have heard the rumors about them. This dice penalty is equal to their Bane Severity. Creating an alternative identity may alleviate this weakness for a night or two, but it too will eventually develop a similar string of rumors. Ravnos can not buy Influence or Status at character creation. </div> </div> </div>This one is based off a quote from the Erciyes Fragments:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He who took no action, but abandoned others to their fate,<br /> Shall be himself outcast, and trusted by no one. </div> </div> </div>Thoughts? Opinions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T18:30:40-08:00","id":1470678,"title":"","content":"The Ravnos shouldn't be Caitiff, with status or influence blocks.<br /> &quot;The clanless are not like the rest of us. Even the Ravnos \u2014 Lilith bless their dozen or so souls \u2014 are defined by something&quot; Fiorenza Savona on the Caitiff<br /> <br /> The first option isn't that bad, except that it makes the Ravnos completely slaves to their compulsions. Second option is broken and pigeonholes the characters into never being social worst than the Nosferatu. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not only that, but it limits playing Ravnos in V5 to only modern timeline, which is also my issue with Tremere, Salubri, and Banu Haquim. </div> </div> </div>Change it from physical, to willpower damage, maybe make it certain instead of a 1/10 chance per bane severity. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T18:45:36-08:00","id":1470679,"title":"","content":"My personal version for the Ravnos is that they must indulge their vice/obsession at least once during the night or lose Bane severity Willpower.<br /> <br /> It gives them a choice to not indulge at a cost rather like the Ventrue being able to feed outside their type at a cost and is similar in some ways to the Tzmisce one for suffering for not being near their charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T10:19:06-08:00","id":1470721,"title":"","content":"I just really like the V20 Vice shtick. The more you think about it, the more fascinating they are, from a sociology perspective. Anything that's not an addiction to vice or at least a compulsion to do something socially harmful is a hard downgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:35:26-08:00","id":1470743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1470721#post1470721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just really like the V20 Vice shtick. The more you think about it, the more fascinating they are, from a sociology perspective. Anything that's not an addiction to vice or at least a compulsion to do something socially harmful is a hard downgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal favorite vice I\u2019ve seen from a PC was \u201cshopaholic.\u201d They continually bought either useless crap they were never going to use or gifts to hand out as needed and oh so many clothes. But when you don\u2019t need food and can have a lifetime of compound interest you can do stuff like that.<br /> <br /> They recently sired a childe who was a real technophile in life and their vice became an addiction to social media and not being able to leave his freaking phone alone even when talking to other people.<br /> <br /> People get too caught up on the idea of vice as a crime and the classic expressions of the Biblical vices that they miss the multitude of completely legal modern vices a Ravnos (particularly since the bulk are going to be childer of the modern nights, having been sired by the survivors of the Week of Nightmares - so 20 years or less as vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T06:56:32-08:00","id":1470782,"title":"","content":"I think the V20 version is less bad than others and the DAV20 an improvement, but I really dislike the compulsion for vices. I like how you handle it, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a>, but I do think it serves them better for the accusations levied against them to be unrelated to their actual actions and proclivities. So I think the second OP option needs a lot of work on it, but is actually in the right direction.<br /> <br /> One option that occurred me is that tying to Chimerstry there may be some sort of Doppelganger effect following the Ravnos. An illusion, either on the real world or just in dreams, does the stuff the Ravnos is blamed for. This thing shouldn't manifest all the time, obviously, but is enough to create and spread rumors about the vampire.<br /> <br /> Maybe the illusion represents other people's desires and fears, but its appearance is always related to the Ravnos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T07:44:53-08:00","id":1470784,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see why a Ravnos\u2019 weakness needs to be any more external than a Brujah\u2019s rage, a Toreador\u2019s fugues in the face of beauty, a Malkavian\u2019s mental illness, or a Ventrue\u2019s refusal to feed on anyone but a specific type.<br /> <br /> The Brujah\u2019s reputation for being hot-headed and violence-prone doesn\u2019t come from some external force making them look bad. It\u2019s because the Beast inside them rages.<br /> <br /> Similarly, there\u2019s no reason for the Ravnos\u2019 reputation to be some supernatural smear campaign against an innocent bystander\u2026 they have the reputation they do because their Beast urges them towards self-destructive actions and no one likes to get caught in someone else\u2019s hot mess.<br /> <br /> The desire to basically absolve the Ravnos of personal sins feels a bit like trying to make up for the past Gypsy stereotypes by making them the opposite instead\u2026 when the real answer is that, post-Week of Nightmares, the majority of Ravnos are just people of numerous backgrounds and ethnicities chosen by the survivors for the Embrace and the Ravnos\u2019 clans personal Beast is one that urges self-destructive behaviors in people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T09:40:26-08:00","id":1470790,"title":"","content":"The vice weakness is my favourite thing about the clan, followed by the bloodlines/&quot;jati&quot; that either revel in it or mitigate it, although it does bring them very close to the Ministry. In V5, it might be a more apt compulsion than bane, but in that case, I can't imagine what bane they should have. Maybe they could be themed around fear like VtR Nosferatu or Begotten Beasts, but would be a whole new concept.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T10:21:07-08:00","id":1470792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1470784#post1470784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see why a Ravnos\u2019 weakness needs to be any more external than a Brujah\u2019s rage, a Toreador\u2019s fugues in the face of beauty, a Malkavian\u2019s mental illness, or a Ventrue\u2019s refusal to feed on anyone but a specific type.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. But that would be a change of pace.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Ravnos' weakness is how encompassing it is, because it sets the character in a pre-defined behavior. A member of any of those clans can deal with their weaknesses in an infinite number of ways. A Ravnos either engage in it or not. At the same time, it can be engaged in any form, so it easily becomes a &quot;Compulsion to do what I would anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I just don't like it. Except for a player/ST coming up with a very clever &quot;vice&quot; as you did, by itself it is the most boring weakness I know of. So I want to engage with the idea of making something new in its place, and an external curse is something not done yet.<br /> <br /> Do I need another reason to throw ideas and see what sticks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T10:37:00-08:00","id":1470794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1470782#post1470782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the V20 version is less bad than others and the DAV20 an improvement, but I really dislike the compulsion for vices. I like how you handle it, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a>, but I do think it serves them better for the accusations levied against them to be unrelated to their actual actions and proclivities. So I think the second OP option needs a lot of work on it, but is actually in the right direction.<br /> <br /> One option that occurred me is that tying to Chimerstry there may be some sort of Doppelganger effect following the Ravnos. An illusion, either on the real world or just in dreams, does the stuff the Ravnos is blamed for. This thing shouldn't manifest all the time, obviously, but is enough to create and spread rumors about the vampire.<br /> <br /> Maybe the illusion represents other people's desires and fears, but its appearance is always related to the Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kind of like the wandering reflection/Ba of the Hollow Mekhet in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T08:34:51-08:00","id":1473263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1470792#post1470792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the Ravnos' weakness is how encompassing it is, because it sets the character in a pre-defined behavior. A member of any of those clans can deal with their weaknesses in an infinite number of ways. A Ravnos either engage in it or not. At the same time, it can be engaged in any form, so it easily becomes a &quot;Compulsion to do what I would anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I just don't like it. Except for a player/ST coming up with a very clever &quot;vice&quot; as you did, by itself it is the most boring weakness I know of.<br /> Do I need another reason to throw ideas and see what sticks?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of ways you can deal with the Ravnos weakness along interesting lines, making the curse either tragic or vicious. The Ravnos weakness is disturbing to the Ravnos themselves, as the urges are both inconvenient and involuntary: unless they are on the Path of Paradox, they have to resist it to some degree, as otherwise they will create a huge disturbance or move around a lot to spread out their predation. They need some sort of ethical framework and build a life around it, similar to how the Brujah deal with their own clan curse. The Ravnos Beast is insidious; it taps into hidden desires and is sometimes similar to a Kuei-jin's Shadow compared to bloodthirstiness of other vampires.<br /> <br /> Consider a Ravnos whose weakness is physical confrontation and assault. Based on the vampire's personality, this could enter his or her consciousness in several ways. The vampire could be angry and vicious and be pressured to vent; it could be a traumatized or insecure upbringing's way of compensationg; or it could be an urge to punish the unrighteous and stupid behavior typically encountered in everyday life. A gangster who corners and beats people for fun is very different than a courier who pursues an example of stupid driving that caused a fender bender and kicks the drunk driver's teeth in to make a point. A high-Humanity Ravnos with this weakness could adopt a Batman-sort of vigilantism, positioning himself to thwart the most dangerous targets, and try to not kill as an outcome of the fighting. A Ravnos could seek out the biggest, toughest bruisers or multiple opponents for such fights, or he could revel in knocking around the weak and helpless. The Ravnos may outright attack other vampires and seek out a scourge-like role in the domain, or he may do his utmost to resist the urge around Kindred, spending willpower, then going off on mortal targets. The Ravnos may use such behavior to disguise his feeding, or not. His ghouls may be or may not be targets for his weakness. The Ravnos with this weakness might have Fortitude as his primary Discipline, and be distinguished by this specialty instead of the stereotypical Chimerstry user. He could be a two-bit punk, or an honorable warrior with high levels of Brawl and Melee. He could be liked and respected in the domain if he compensates right, and could be a hated outcast if he does not comport himself well. He might choose to cover up his attacks, or not. He could see other Ravnos as fellow criminals, or have no sympathy for vices such as compulsive lying or pointless theft. He might have a strong clan identity, or he could be the sort whose clan is indistinguishable at first glance, belonging to a mixed coterie and not having his behavior stand out.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos weakness is one of the best clan curses for crafting good characters; the lack of official good writing in the setting just means that the players have to do some original thinking, rather than having the concepts be served on a silver platter like with the other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T23:23:10-08:00","id":1473320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1473263#post1473263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ravnos weakness is one of the best clan curses for crafting good characters; the lack of official good writing in the setting just means that the players have to do some original thinking, rather than having the concepts be served on a silver platter like with the other clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb I refrain from praising a rule for increasing the workload of ST or players.<br /> <br /> It is <b>not</b> a good clan curse to craft good characters precisely because it demands the player to be already able to craft a good character. If the player has this ability, I can guarantee you this player can craft a good character out of any clan. And yes, this player, if so inclined, can make the weakness work despite being badly written.<br /> <br /> But this is a formalized system, professionally written, for consumption and use by a large pool of people. The job of the system is to provide those people with the tools they need to make good games without having to be almost professionals themselves. If something in the system demands greater ability from the consumer, then the system failed as such.<br /> <br /> This by no means signify that having a good game with bad rules is impossible if the players and/or ST are good, it just means that the quality of such experience isn't a merit of the system, and here I'm talking about the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T08:21:37-08:00","id":1473331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1473320#post1473320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, this player, if so inclined, can make the weakness work despite being badly written.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weakness is not badly written (referring to Revised, not the rest), it merely lacks enough writing, to make the players aware of the prospects. Anybody who played Bloodlines can immediately run Brujah, Malkavians, Nosferatu etc. But there just weren't enough significant Ravnos characters developed before VtM was wrapped up. Outside the clanbook, there's only one thoroughly-crafted character, Khalil, and one Methuselah, Hazimel. Durga Syn and a handful of others were only ever used in the books as plot devices. They never got around to writing a Delhi by Night, which would have been awesome, and would have taken place in a majority-Ravnos setting. I mean, even in VtM:Redemption, there was an example of every single clan including Giovanni and Assamites, but no Ravnos. What Clan Ravnos needs therefore is not a mechanics overhaul, but a few more well-crafted characters so that players can easily appreciate what the clan has to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T06:43:49-08:00","id":1473401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sultanabdal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470673-v5-alternative-ravnos-bane?p=1473331#post1473331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weakness is not badly written (referring to Revised, not the rest), it merely lacks enough writing, to make the players aware of the prospects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but otherwise I disagree with you for the things you said yourself.<br /> <br /> The quality of the weakness <i><b><u>as a mechanic</u></b></i> isn't in the sample characters. As I said, you can make awesome character out of anything, and I mean it. The quality of the weakness is measured by how easy it is for an amateur to craft an interesting character out of what is given in the <u><b>core book alone</b></u>.<br /> <br /> If you need more material to make it work as fodder for that amateur, then the core did a bad job, either because it was badly worded or because the mechanic itself isn't that good.<br /> <br /> An amateur shouldn't need Delhi by Night to make an interesting Ravnos. I've seen throughout the years scores of interesting characters, even if not great, created by newbies with just passing familiarity with the core's description of each clan and nothing more, frequently right after acquiring such familiarity, especially when I worked at anime events presenting classic RPG materials to event goers unfamiliar with the hobby.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is the only clan I've never saw done well by someone without both a lot of knowledge of the game and experience at creating interesting characters, at least when exploring their weakness, because for every clan you always have the option of ignoring the weakness altogether when creating the character and then just slapping it in as an afterthought. You'll have an interesting character, but it will be despite the weakness, not because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}